//! The `font-variant` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property allows you to set all the font variants for a font.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - all-petite-caps: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps`
//! longhand property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the
//! `font` shorthand property.
//! - all-small-caps: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps`
//! longhand property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the
//! `font` shorthand property.
//! - emoji: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-emoji` longhand
//! property.
//! - historical-forms: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-ligatures`
//! longhand property.
//! - none: Sets the value of the `font-variant-ligatures` as `none` and the values of the other
//! longhand properties as `normal`, their initial value.
//! - normal: Specifies a normal font face. Each longhand property has an initial value of `normal`.
//! - ordinal: Specifies the keywords related to the `font-variant-numeric` longhand property. The
//! possible values are `lining-nums`, `oldstyle-nums`, `proportional-nums`, `tabular-nums`,
//! `diagonal-fractions`, `stacked-fractions`, `ordinal`, and `slashed-zero`.
//! - petite-caps: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps` longhand
//! property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the `font`
//! shorthand property.
//! - ruby: Specifies the keywords related to the `font-variant-east-asian` longhand property. The
//! possible values are `jis78`, `jis83`, `jis90`, `jis04`, `simplified`, `traditional`,
//! `full-width`, `proportional-width`, and `ruby`.
//! - slashed-zero: Specifies the keywords related to the `font-variant-numeric` longhand property.
//! The possible values are `lining-nums`, `oldstyle-nums`, `proportional-nums`, `tabular-nums`,
//! `diagonal-fractions`, `stacked-fractions`, `ordinal`, and `slashed-zero`.
//! - small-caps: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps` longhand
//! property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the `font`
//! shorthand property.
//! - sub: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-position` longhand
//! property.
//! - super: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-position` longhand
//! property.
//! - text: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-emoji` longhand
//! property.
//! - titling-caps: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps` longhand
//! property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the `font`
//! shorthand property.
//! - unicase: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-caps` longhand
//! property. The `small-caps` value is the only non-`normal` font variant valid within the `font`
//! shorthand property.
//! - unicode: Specifies the keywords and functions related to the `font-variant-emoji` longhand
//! property.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | none | [ [ <common-lig-values> || <discretionary-lig-values> ||
//! <historical-lig-values> || <contextual-alt-values> ] || [ small-caps | all-small-caps |
//! petite-caps | all-petite-caps | unicase | titling-caps ] || [
//! stylistic(<font-feature-value-name>) || historical-forms || styleset(<font-feature-value-name>#)
//! || character-variant(<font-feature-value-name>#) || swash(<font-feature-value-name>) ||
//! ornaments(<font-feature-value-name>) || annotation(<font-feature-value-name>) ] || [
//! <numeric-figure-values> || <numeric-spacing-values> || <numeric-fraction-values> || ordinal ||
//! slashed-zero ] || [ <east-asian-variant-values> || <east-asian-width-values> || ruby ] || [ sub |
//! super ] || [ text | emoji | unicode ] ]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-variant
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-variant
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

